# Fleet A/B radio config overlay (openmanet_setup.sh ... -x mm6108only).
#
# Two jobs, both strand-critical for the shared A/B rootfs:
#
# 1) mm6108-only: the A/B golden reuses ONE build_dir root.squashfs across both
#    slots, so the rootfs must carry a single S1G radio driver. Shipping both
#    mm6108 and mm8108 makes the driver refuse to load ("morse_sdio already
#    registered"). ekh-bcm2711/target_diffconfig enables all three device
#    profiles with per-device strips (correct for per-device .img, wrong for the
#    shared rootfs), so strip mm8108 globally here.
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-mm8108 is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_mm8108-firmware is not set
# CONFIG_TARGET_DEVICE_bcm27xx_bcm2711_DEVICE_bcm2711_mm8108-usb is not set
#
# 2) Bake the Pi on-board wifi (brcmfmac) INTO the image as =y. The board config
#    leaves these as =m (built but NOT installed in the squashfs -- verified: the
#    manifest omits them). brcmfmac must occupy radio0 so morse (HaLow) stays
#    radio1, matching fleet p5 layout; without it morse drops to radio0 and OTA
#    strands seeded mesh nodes. =m + MODULE_DEFAULT is NOT enough; force =y.
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-brcmfmac=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_brcmfmac-nvram-43455-sdio=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_cypress-firmware-43455-sdio=y
